      "problem": "Suppose $|\\,c\\,|=18$ and the angle between vectors $c$ and $d$ is $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$ Find the scalar projection of $c$ onto $d.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =|\\,c\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =18\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =18\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-9\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
